# UI descriptions are static data. This library deliberately has no renderer.
# All section patterns and the descriptor representation are editable here.
import lib/sections.dl
import lib/callbacks.dl
import lib/check.dl
import appearance.dl
import text_states.dl

class:
    patterns:
        UI element
    members:
        kind as an integer
        text as a C string
        color as a C string
        columns as an integer
        rows as an integer
        border as an integer
        children as a pointer to a pointer to UI element
        count as an integer
        action as a pointer
        left as an integer
        top as an integer
        width as an integer
        height as an integer
        variant as a C string
        appearance as UI appearance reference
        content as a C string
        destination as a C string
        read only as a boolean

UI reference means: a pointer to UI element
default UI cell width means: 220
default UI cell height means: 48
no UI children means: @intrinsic("construct", UI reference array of 0 items)
UI children of values means: @intrinsic("cast", a static reference to values, a pointer to UI reference)
no UI action means: @intrinsic("construct", a pointer)

UI node {integer:kind} with {C string:text} colored {C string:color} sized {integer:columns} by {integer:rows} bordered {integer:border} containing {an array:children} acting {a pointer:action} at {integer:left} {integer:top} measuring {integer:width} by {integer:height} styled {C string:variant} means: a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI element, kind, text, color, columns, rows, border, UI children of children, the length of children, action, left, top, width, height, variant, no UI appearance, text, "", false)
UI node {integer:kind} with {C string:text} colored {C string:color} sized {integer:columns} by {integer:rows} bordered {integer:border} containing {an array:children} acting {a pointer:action} means: UI node kind with text colored color sized columns by rows bordered border containing children acting action at 0 0 measuring 0 by 0 styled ""
a UI container of kind {integer:kind} containing {an array:children} means: UI node kind with "" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing children acting no UI action

{UI reference:node} wearing {UI appearance reference:appearance} means: a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI element, node's kind, node's text, node's color, node's columns, node's rows, node's border, node's children, node's count, node's action, node's left, node's top, node's width, node's height, node's variant, appearance, node's content, node's destination, node's read only)
{UI reference:node} with initial text {C string:content} means: a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI element, node's kind, node's text, node's color, node's columns, node's rows, node's border, node's children, node's count, node's action, node's left, node's top, node's width, node's height, node's variant, node's appearance, content, node's destination, node's read only)
{UI reference:node} leading to {C string:destination} means: a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI element, node's kind, node's text, node's color, node's columns, node's rows, node's border, node's children, node's count, node's action, node's left, node's top, node's width, node's height, node's variant, node's appearance, node's content, destination, node's read only)
{UI reference:node} with read only text means: a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI element, node's kind, node's text, node's color, node's columns, node's rows, node's border, node's children, node's count, node's action, node's left, node's top, node's width, node's height, node's variant, node's appearance, node's content, node's destination, true)

button {C string:label} means: UI node 2 with label colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
col {C string:label} means: UI node 5 with label colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
label {C string:text} means: UI node 11 with text colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action

implicitly convert {C string:label}:
    replacement:
        col label

section window {name}:
    declares: name
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 0 with name colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

section toolbar:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 1 with "" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

section {integer:columns} x {integer:rows} table:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 3 with "" colored "" sized columns by rows bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

section {C string:color} row:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 4 with "" colored color sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

section style:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 6 with "" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

tables are {C string:color} means: UI node 7 with "" colored color sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
table cells are {integer:width} x {integer:height} pixels means: UI node 8 with "" colored "" sized width by height bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
buttons are {C string:color} and have a {integer:width} [pixel|pixels] border means: UI node 9 with "" colored color sized 0 by 0 bordered width containing no UI children acting no UI action

class:
    patterns:
        UI handler
    members:
        target as UI reference
        action as a pointer
        context as a pointer
        next as a pointer to UI handler
        event as an integer

class:
    patterns:
        UI value
    members:
        target as UI reference
        text state as UI text state
        number as an integer
        next as a pointer to UI value
        destination as a string
        enabled as a boolean
        read only as a boolean
        text protected as a boolean

{UI value:entry}'s text means: entry's text state's text
{a pointer to UI value:entry}'s text means: entry's text state's text
{UI value:entry}'s undo means: entry's text state's undo
{a pointer to UI value:entry}'s undo means: entry's text state's undo
{UI value:entry}'s redo means: entry's text state's redo
{a pointer to UI value:entry}'s redo means: entry's text state's redo
{UI value:entry}'s colored text means: entry's text state's colored text
{a pointer to UI value:entry}'s colored text means: entry's text state's colored text
{UI value:entry}'s colors means: entry's text state's colors
{a pointer to UI value:entry}'s colors means: entry's text state's colors
{UI value:entry}'s last color means: entry's text state's last color
{a pointer to UI value:entry}'s last color means: entry's text state's last color
{UI value:entry}'s mark layers means: entry's text state's mark layers
{a pointer to UI value:entry}'s mark layers means: entry's text state's mark layers

class:
    patterns:
        UI observer
    members:
        context as a pointer
        notify as a pointer
        next as a pointer to UI observer

class:
    patterns:
        UI instance
    members:
        description as UI reference
        state as a pointer
        status as a string
        handlers as a pointer to UI handler
        values as a pointer to UI value
        page as UI reference
        reduced motion as a boolean
        revision as an integer
        observers as a pointer to UI observer
        event target as UI reference
        event context as a pointer

to invalidate {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    increment instance's revision
    set observer to instance's observers
    loop while observer != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI observer):
        @intrinsic("call pointer", observer's notify, nothing, observer's context)
        set observer to observer's next

this window means: @intrinsic("receiver")

section code:
    receiver: a pointer to UI instance
    returns: nothing
    result: UI reference
    value:
        UI node 10 with "" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting @intrinsic("cast", @intrinsic("deferred body"), a pointer)

section when the {C string:label} button is clicked:
    receiver: a pointer to UI instance
    returns: nothing
    value:
        bind the button labeled label in this window to @intrinsic("deferred body")

to get the UI child at {integer:index} in {UI reference:parent}:
    return the item at index in (parent's children)

# Tree lookup is independent of the concrete section patterns above.
to get the element of kind {integer:kind} labeled {C string:label} in {UI reference:root}:
    if root's kind = kind and root's text = label:
        return root
    set index to 0
    loop while index < root's count:
        set found to the element of kind kind labeled label in (the UI child at index in root)
        if found != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
            return found
        increment index
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)

to get the {C string:label} button in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set found to the element of kind 2 labeled label in (instance's description)
    if found = @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
        abort the program
    return found

the {C string:label} button means: the label button in this window

to bind the button labeled {C string:label} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance} to {a callback:action}:
    set target to (the label button in instance)
    bind UI action action to target in instance for event 0 with context @intrinsic("construct", a pointer)

to get [the UI handler for] {UI reference:target} [in] {a pointer to UI instance:instance} [for event] {integer:event}:
    set handler to instance's handlers
    loop while handler != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
        if (handler's target = target) and (handler's event = event):
            return handler
        set handler to handler's next
    return @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler)

to [bind UI action] {a callback:action} [to] {UI reference:target} [in] {a pointer to UI instance:instance} [for event] {integer:event} [with context] {a pointer:context}:
    set handler to the UI handler for target in instance for event event
    set callback to @intrinsic("cast", action, a pointer)
    if handler != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
        # Opaque byte pointers need identity; = compares C-string contents.
        if @intrinsic("equal", handler's action, callback) and @intrinsic("equal", handler's context, context):
            return nothing
        set handler's action to callback
        set handler's context to context
    else:
        set entry to @intrinsic("construct", UI handler, target, callback, context, instance's handlers, event)
        set instance's handlers to storage for one slot initialized with entry
    invalidate instance

to [unbind UI handlers with context] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    # The supplied owner can itself be a field of a released handler.
    set owner to context
    set handler to instance's handlers
    set previous to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler)
    set changed to false
    loop while handler != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
        set next to handler's next
        if @intrinsic("equal", handler's context, owner):
            if previous = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
                set instance's handlers to next
            else:
                set previous's next to next
            deallocate handler
            set changed to true
        else:
            set previous to handler
        set handler to next
    if changed:
        invalidate instance

to [invoke UI handler] {a pointer to UI handler:handler} [for] {UI reference:target} [in] {a pointer to UI instance:instance} [receiving] {a value:receiver}:
    # A callback may replace or remove its own registration.
    set action to handler's action
    set context to handler's context
    set {previous target} to instance's event target
    set {previous context} to instance's event context
    set instance's event target to target
    set instance's event context to context
    @intrinsic("call pointer", action, nothing, receiver)
    set instance's event target to previous target
    set instance's event context to previous context

to initialize {a pointer to UI instance:instance} from {UI reference:node}:
    if node's kind = 10:
        @intrinsic("call pointer", node's action, nothing, instance)
    set index to 0
    loop while index < node's count:
        initialize instance from (the UI child at index in node)
        increment index

to get an instance of {UI reference:description} with state {a pointer to a value:state}:
    set result to a new UI instance
    set result's description to description
    set result's state to @intrinsic("cast", state, a pointer)
    set result's status to "Ready"
    initialize the address of result from description
    return result

to get an instance of {UI reference:description}:
    return an instance of description with state (0 as a pointer to a byte)

to get the UI element {UI reference:node} is enabled in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set value to instance's values
    loop while value != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI value):
        if value's target = node:
            return value's enabled
        set value to value's next
    return true

to click {UI reference:button} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    if (the UI element button is enabled in instance) = false:
        return nothing
    set handler to the UI handler for button in instance for event 0
    if handler != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
        invoke UI handler handler for button in instance receiving instance
        invalidate instance

to click the {C string:label} button in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    click (the label button in instance) in instance

to close {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    require condition (instance's observers = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI observer)) reporting "Close the UI views before closing their instance"
    set handler to instance's handlers
    loop while handler != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
        set next to handler's next
        deallocate handler
        set handler to next
    set instance's handlers to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler)
    set value to instance's values
    loop while value != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI value):
        set next to value's next
        clear UI text state (the address of (value's text state))
        destroy the value at value
        deallocate value
        set value to next
    set instance's values to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI value)

to release UI text colors {a pointer to UI value:value}:
    release UI text colors (the address of (value's text state))

to release UI text marks {a pointer to UI value:value}:
    release UI text marks (the address of (value's text state))

class:
    patterns:
        UI selection
    members:
        element as UI reference
        root as UI reference

to get the table of {UI reference:root}:
    set found to the element of kind 3 labeled "" in root
    require condition (found != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)) reporting "This UI description has no table"
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI selection, found, root)

{UI reference:root}'s table means: the table of root

to get the {C string:color} row of {UI selection:table}:
    set index to 0
    loop while index < table's element's count:
        set entry to the UI child at index in (table's element)
        if entry's kind = 4 and entry's color = color:
            return @intrinsic("construct", UI selection, entry, table's root)
        increment index
    abort the program
    return a new UI selection

to get the UI cell width in {UI reference:root}:
    set rule to the element of kind 8 labeled "" in root
    if rule = @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
        return default UI cell width
    return rule's columns

to get the width of {UI selection:row}:
    return (the table of row's root)'s element's columns * (the UI cell width in (row's root))
